remediation = Character remediation
remediation-blocked = These corrections await Game contract acceptance. Review a correction to see the required evidence and controls.
remediation-target = Eligible target and current revisions
remediation-preview = Verified dry-run preview
remediation-approval = Independent approval bound to the preview
remediation-receipt = Verified Game receipt
remediation-controls-R2 = Requires staff MFA, the operation grant, current world scope, a reason code and a case reference.
remediation-controls-R3 = Requires staff MFA, the operation grant, current world scope, a reason code, a case reference and requester step-up within five minutes. A Game dry run must be supported.
remediation-controls-R4 = Requires staff MFA, the operation grant, current world scope, a reason code, a case reference and requester step-up within five minutes. Execution also requires a verified Game preview and a different, independently scoped approver. Approval must be under 30 minutes old and follow approver step-up within five minutes.
remediation-rescue = Rescue a stuck character
remediation-rescue-evidence = Game must verify the character and channel, location revision, stuck evidence, safe destination and policy revision, movement restrictions and the current session generation when online.
remediation-rescue-receipt = The receipt identifies the resolved destination, redacted prior location and resulting location revision.
remediation-disconnect = Disconnect one character session
remediation-disconnect-evidence = Game must verify the channel, exact active session ID, generation and revision before terminating that generation and invalidating its reconnect proofs.
remediation-disconnect-receipt = The receipt confirms durable termination and proof invalidation for the exact session generation, with an end time and event reference.
remediation-outfit = Correct an outfit
remediation-outfit-evidence = Game must verify the selected outfit, colours, add-ons and optional mount against content, appearance and entitlement revisions, case evidence and owned cosmetics.
remediation-outfit-receipt = The receipt confirms the accepted appearance and resulting revisions. Audit retains the restricted reference to the recoverable prior appearance.
remediation-compensate = Compensate for a lost item
remediation-compensate-evidence = Game must verify the item definition, requested quantity, inventory and definition revisions, provenance and correction line, and the canonical loss revision and remaining allowance.
remediation-compensate-receipt = The receipt records the applied quantity, affected items or restricted manifest, resulting revisions and Game ledger reference.
remediation-confiscate = Confiscate an item
remediation-confiscate-evidence = Game must verify the exact item instance, location and custody revision, definition and inventory revisions, quantity, provenance and correction line. Moved or escrowed items are ineligible.
remediation-confiscate-receipt = The receipt records the applied quantity, affected items or restricted manifest, resulting inventory and custody revisions and Game ledger reference.
